{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Decompose PydanticAIRunner.run() along its real seams\n\nImplements ADR 0056 (`docs/adr/0056-decompose-pydantic-ai-runner-run.md`). Read it first — every\ndecision, every rejected alternative, and the corrections an adversarial review forced are recorded\nthere with measured evidence.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe RUNNER CLUSTER only: `runner.py` and the modules already split out of it — `structured_run.py`,\n`providers.py`, `capabilities.py`, `anthropic_model.py`.\n\nExplicitly OUT of scope: a project-wide per-function length gate (it would affect 62 functions across\nsix subsystems — see ADR 0056 decision 1, which records the measurement and the residual risk), and\n`config.py` (a sibling, never split from runner, with a differently-shaped problem).\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nrunner.py has been split THREE times — `c1f4` (−146), task 2682 (−152), task 3a98 (−35) — and sits at\n689 lines, **782 with task cc33 pending** against an 800 hard cap. Ticket 1484 relieved the identical\npressure in `gate_dispatch.py` and `orchestrator.py` weeks earlier.\n\nMEASURED at 97791145f: `PydanticAIRunner.run()` spans 219–626 = **408 lines, 59% of the file**\n(227 code, 166 comment, 15 blank). Every prior split extracted a CALLEE — which always satisfies a\nper-FILE gate while leaving the calling method untouched. So the method keeps absorbing work and the\nfile regrows. We split the nouns while the pressure sat on the verb.\n\nA VERIFIED latent defect makes this urgent rather than cosmetic: `ProviderSession(cfg)` is\nconstructed at runner.py:301 but the `try` guarding it starts at 474, with `finally: close()` at 582.\nLines 301–473 are OUTSIDE the guard and several raise by design, leaking an opened\n`httpx.AsyncClient`. `ProviderSession.__enter__`/`__exit__` exist (providers.py:295–299) and are\nnever used, while providers.py:21 documents a `with ProviderSession(...)` caller that does not exist.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract PLAIN FUNCTIONS with explicit parameters — deliberately NOT the frozen `ResolvedCall` carrier\nan earlier draft proposed. Review established that two of its seven fields are mutated after\nconstruction (task cc33 writes `provider_provenance[\"ran_model\"]` after the `finally`), so the freeze\nwould be decorative exactly where it matters, at ~30–40 lines of `replace()` ceremony to relocate\n~113 lines of code.\n\nOrder is set by measured code density and by where growth actually landed, NOT by tidiness: the\n`except` spine first (75 lines at 20% comment = 58 code), then the settings block (80 lines at 55%\ncomment = 36 code).\n\n## Sequencing constraint (CORRECTED — the original was circular)\n\nThe first version of this section said \"LAND NOTHING HERE UNTIL TASK cc33 MERGES\". That was WRONG\nand CI proved it: cc33's +97 lines put runner.py at 782, which fails task 3a98's headroom guard\n(`test_structured_run_seam.py::test_runner_regains_real_headroom_under_the_cap`, asserting < 700).\nSo cc33 could not merge until this work landed, while this work was told to wait for cc33 — a\ndeadlock.\n\nThe real requirement was never \"wait for cc33 to merge\". It was **do not AUTHOR against a pre-cc33\nbase**, because the diff would be wrong — cc33 touches four of the regions these children move.\ncc33 is now cherry-picked INTO the working stack (a3c4fd472), so that condition is already met:\nthese children extract the POST-cc33 code, in the same stack, with no rebase conflict.\n\n### EVERY CHANGE MUST CLEAR THE 700 GUARD ON ITS OWN (measured; corrects the arithmetic below)\n\nAn earlier version of this section reasoned that e6bd could land at 707 — over the guard — because\n8229 would bring the STACK green. **That is false, and it would have wedged the whole stack.**\nMEASURED in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`: CI checks out the EXACT PATCHSET\n(`checkout-gerrit-change-action` with `gerrit-refspec: refs/changes/NN/NNNN/P`) and runs the full\nsuite per change, casting `Verified` per change. A relation chain cannot be submitted with a red\nancestor, so an intermediate commit at 707 is `Verified -1` and blocks e6bd, 8229 and everything\nabove them.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: each child's own commit must leave runner.py under 700. The per-child arithmetic:\n\n    782  current, with cc33 in the stack\n    -75  e6bd  (the except spine)     -> 707 by the ADR's estimate; MEASURED 718 for the pure\n                                         extraction, so e6bd must recover the remainder inside its\n                                         own change to clear 700\n    -80  8229  (the settings block)   -> ~620\n\nNote that NEITHER extraction alone clears 700 from 782 by its headline figure (782−80 = 702 for 8229\ntoo). The tightness is not an artifact of the ordering.\n\nWhere a child needs extra relief inside its own change, it may TIGHTEN COMMENT WORDING in `run()`\n(the pre-call region is 50% comment) but **must not drop a measured number, a `file:line` citation, a\nbug/story/epic id, a named failure mode, or a stated invariant.** Deleting documentation to satisfy a\nsize guard is the same species of move as raising the cap, which ADR 0056 rejects by name. If the\nfacts cannot fit, stop and re-plan rather than delete one.\n\n**Do NOT relax the guard.** Lowering a threshold that exists to catch exactly this regrowth is the\n\"raise the cap\" anti-pattern ADR 0056 rejects by name, and it would discard the one mechanism that\ncaught it.\n\n## Stack order\n\nBottom to top, on the existing stack above change 1104:\n\n    e6bd   (except spine)      — must land first; 8229 depends on it\n    8229   (settings block)    — depends on e6bd\n    a49e   (session guard)     — depends on 8229\n\nThese edges are RECORDED as blocking links (`e6bd blocks 8229`, `8229 blocks a49e`), not merely\ndescribed here, so the stack order cannot drift.\n\na49e sits on top DELIBERATELY. It is LOC-neutral (it swaps a construct-plus-`finally` for a `with`),\nso it can only satisfy the 700 guard by inheriting the relief e6bd and 8229 already landed beneath\nit. **If the extractions are descoped, a49e cannot simply be re-based to land alone**: on the 782\nbase it would be ~782 and fail the guard. Landing it alone requires either its own source of relief\nor an explicit operator override of the size gate — it is not a free-standing change, and an earlier\ndraft of this section wrongly implied it was.\n\n## What this story does NOT reach (honest residual)\n\nADR 0056 names FOUR extractions: `interpret_failure`, `build_model_settings`, `build_usage_limits`,\n`build_agent_kwargs`. This story's three children cover the first three. `build_agent_kwargs` and the\npre-call/telemetry regions are NOT covered here, so this story lands runner.py at roughly 620 and\n`run()` at roughly 250 lines — NOT the ADR's projected ≈470-on-the-cc33-base file with a 60–90 line\n`run()`.\n\nThat remainder is real work, not a rounding error, and is tracked as follow-up rather than silently\ndropped: **task 5e75-522e-70d1-4363 (clay-nutty-housefly)**, linked `discovered_from` this story,\ncarries the `build_agent_kwargs` and telemetry extractions. It is deliberately a LINKED ticket and\nNOT a child, so it does not gate this story's close. AC2 below is stated at the bound this story's\nOWN children actually reach; the ADR's projection stays the longer-term target for 5e75.\n\n## Known migration hazard\n\n\"Zero test edits\" does NOT hold here, unlike ticket 1484. Six string-keyed\n`monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, …)` targets move: `cache_settings_for`, `_pai_model` (×3),\n`_local_proxy_bypass_base_url`, `ProviderSession`, `_pai_structured`. Re-importing a moved name back\ninto `runner` fixes `from … import` callers but NOT `setattr` patches, which rebind `runner`'s global\nwhile the extracted function resolves through its own module globals.\n\nMEASURED mitigation: neutering the `cache_settings_for` patch makes\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` fail LOUDLY\n(`ImportError: cannot import name 'ModelHTTPError' from 'pydantic_ai'`), not pass silently. So these\nbreakages are visible. An adversarial review predicted a silent pass here; running it showed\notherwise, which is why each child requires the repoint to land in the same commit as its extraction.\n\nMEASURED for e6bd specifically: NONE of the eight `monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, …)` targets in the\nsuite (`_import_pydantic_ai`, `_local_proxy_bypass_base_url`, `_pai_model`, `_pai_structured`,\n`cache_settings_for`, `capabilities_for`, `get_runner`, `ProviderSession`) lies in the except spine,\nso that child needs zero repoints. The hazard lands on the LATER children.\n\n### a49e OWNS EXACTLY ONE REPOINT — VERIFIED IN SOURCE, and it is not a `setattr` rebind\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:111` defines a stub\n`_NoBuildProviderSession` that is installed with\n`monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"ProviderSession\", _NoBuildProviderSession)` at line 124. MEASURED:\nthat stub implements `__init__`, `supports`, `is_resolvable` and `close` — and **NOT** `__enter__` /\n`__exit__`. The moment a49e introduces `with ProviderSession(cfg) as provider_session:`, the stub\nstops satisfying the context-manager protocol and that test fails at runtime.\n\n**a49e must give `_NoBuildProviderSession` an `__enter__` (returning `self`) and an `__exit__`\n(calling `self.close()`) IN THE SAME COMMIT that introduces the `with`.** This is a stub gaining the\nprotocol the real object already has (`providers.py:295–299`), not a weakened assertion, so it is\ncompatible with the \"no test ASSERTION changed\" criterion below.\n\nNote this repoint is a DIFFERENT failure mode from the six `setattr`-rebind hazards above: nothing\nmoved modules, so re-importing a name fixes nothing. It is the stub's INTERFACE that fell behind the\ncall site. Do not go looking for a module-globals explanation for it.\n\nSAFE, do not over-correct: `_TOOL_CAPABILITY_CHECKED` and `_TEMPERATURE_WITHDRAWN_LOGGED` are\nmodule-level sets mutated via `.clear()` through an import alias — those survive a move untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every child ticket is closed\n- [ ] `runner.py` is under 650 LOC and `PydanticAIRunner.run()` is under 260 lines, both MEASURED in\n      the close comment. These are the bounds THIS story's three children actually reach (see\n      \"honest residual\"); ADR 0056's ≈470/60–90 projection requires the `build_agent_kwargs` and\n      telemetry extractions, which are tracked as a separate follow-up child and are NOT gated here\n- [ ] EVERY child's commit, AS STACKED IN THE ORDER ABOVE, leaves `runner.py` under 700 — measured\n      locally on that child's own commit before push and RECORDED in its commit message, because\n      `Verified` is cast per patchset and a red ancestor blocks the whole relation chain. (\"As\n      stacked\" is the operative phrase: a49e is LOC-neutral and clears the guard only by inheriting\n      e6bd's and 8229's relief, so this is not a claim that any child clears 700 from the 782 base.)\n- [ ] a49e's commit adds `__enter__`/`__exit__` to the `_NoBuildProviderSession` stub in\n      `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py`, in the same commit as the `with`\n- [ ] no comment in `run()` lost a measured number, a `file:line` citation, a bug/story/epic id, a\n      named failure mode, or a stated invariant — wording may be tightened, facts may not be dropped\n- [ ] the provider session is closed on EVERY path including a raise in the pre-call window, asserted\n      by a test that fails against today's code\n- [ ] the full suite passes with no test ASSERTION changed; every monkeypatch repoint is named in its\n      own commit message with the reason"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785516652740610001,"uuid":"b93f43e5-ee7c-4f5f-b16e-d55a3cb336f1"}